App Studio Planning Prompt

"Create a multi-vendor agricultural marketplace app connecting African smallholder farmers and cooperatives directly with buyers, eliminating middlemen and improving price transparency. Core features:

1. Farmer & cooperative profiles — individual farmers can list produce independently or join a cooperative to pool listings and meet bulk order minimums.
2. Product catalog — crop listings with quantity, harvest date, location, quality grade, and price; support both spot listings and pre-harvest offtake contracts buyers can commit to in advance.
3. Price discovery board — a view of recent sale prices by crop and region, so farmers can see market rates before negotiating.
4. Order & transaction tracking — order status from confirmation through delivery (harvested → in transit → delivered), with a simple log farmers can update even on low connectivity.
5. Supply chain traceability — each sale creates a batch/lot record showing farmer or cooperative origin, harvest date, and any quality grading, viewable by the buyer.
6. Buyer-side discovery and filtering — search/filter by crop, region, quantity, and quality grade.
7. In-app messaging — direct farmer-buyer communication for negotiation and delivery coordination.
8. Offline-friendly design — listings and order updates should queue locally and sync when connectivity returns.

Payments should use Pi payment integration for direct farmer-buyer transactions (no lending, credit, or loan features). Prioritize a simple, low-literacy-friendly UI with icon-based navigation and support for local languages.

---

Data model (core entities and relationships)

User
- user_id
- name
- phone/pi_id
- role (farmer / cooperative_admin / buyer)
- region
- language
- kyc_status

Cooperative
- coop_id
- name
- region
- lead_user_id (FK → User)
- Members: many-to-many join table coop_members (coop_id, user_id)

Farm/Listing Source
- source_id
- owner_id (FK → User, the individual farmer)
- coop_id (nullable FK → Cooperative, if listing under a coop)
- A listing can belong to either a solo farmer or a cooperative — this field decides which

Listing
- listing_id
- source_id (FK)
- crop_type
- quantity
- unit
- quality_grade
- harvest_date
- price_per_unit
- listing_type (spot / pre-harvest offtake)
- status (active / sold / expired)

Offtake Contract (for pre-harvest commitments)
- contract_id
- listing_id (FK)
- buyer_id (FK → User)
- agreed_quantity
- agreed_price
- expected_delivery_date
- status (pending / fulfilled / cancelled)

Order
- order_id
- listing_id (FK)
- buyer_id (FK → User)
- seller_source_id (FK → Farm/Listing Source)
- quantity
- total_price
- status (confirmed / harvested / in_transit / delivered)
- created_at
- updated_at
- status changes are what drives your order-tracking UI

Traceability Record (batch/lot)
- batch_id
- order_id (FK)
- source_id (FK)
- harvest_date
- quality_grade_at_pickup
- graded_by (nullable — inspector/buyer user_id)
- notes
- One batch per order fulfillment; this is what the buyer sees as provenance

Price History (for the price discovery board)
- price_record_id
- crop_type
- region
- price_per_unit
- date
- source (derived from completed Order records)
- Populated automatically each time an Order is marked delivered — no separate manual entry needed

Message
- message_id
- order_id or listing_id (FK, context)
- sender_id
- receiver_id
- content
- timestamp

Payment Transaction
- tx_id
- order_id (FK)
- payer_id
- payee_id
- amount
- pi_tx_reference
- status (pending / completed / failed)

Notes / Implementation considerations
- Offline queuing: Listing changes, order updates, and messages should be queued locally with conflict resolution on sync.
- Low-literacy UI: Use icons, short text, and local language translations.
- Pi payments: store pi_id on User and link Payment Transaction to Pi tx references. No credit/loan records.
